          "title": "You'll want to know: praemium, praemiī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "praemium, praemiī — \"a prize, a reward\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Praemium magnum erat: centum dēnāriī. The prize was large: a hundred denarii."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter. First booty taken before others, then any reward. English premium."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "praemium is built on prae, \"before\", and emō, \"to take, to buy\" (EtymDB, Lewis & Short): what one takes before others. English premium comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
